@* Blazor's event handlers and two-way binding are directive attributes contributed by tag helpers in
   Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web, and a tag helper only applies where its namespace is in scope.
   Without this file the Razor compiler does not recognize @onclick, @bind, @oninput, @onchange or
   @onkeydown and emits each one as a literal HTML attribute, silently -- nothing in the build says so.
   Keep these usings; a component that compiles with a dead click handler is worse than one that fails. *@
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Forms
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Routing
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using Microsoft.JSInterop
@using MartenStudio
@using MartenStudio.Components.Shared
@using MartenStudio.Services
